# Import without burning Cursor quota

Cursor weekly quota is charged for agent model turns and tool loops, not for fetching `t.me` or writing D1/R2. Bulk import must not be orchestrated inside a long Cloud Agent session.

## Do

- Run import/seed scripts on a local machine or CI (`scripts/import-awesome`, `scripts/seed/seed.ts`). The agent may start a command and report a short summary only.
- Keep row content out of chat: no per-entry SQL, profile text, or avatar base64 through MCP or the conversation.
- Follow `import-quality.mdc` before any D1 write (hard rejects and optional clef-omni quality node in the script, not in chat).
- Default: write D1 rows first; leave avatars, recent posts, and member history to the every-5-minutes refresh cron. When the user explicitly wants media with the import, use `seed.ts --remote` (or the same local fetch→R2 path) so bytes never pass through the agent dialogue.
- Prefer keyword taxonomy rules; call `@cf/cloudflare/clef-omni` for blank categories and for **borderline quality only** (Workers AI cost, not Cursor).
- Keep agent sessions short: give an instruction, stop, open a new short session to check progress later.

## Do not

- Do not drive hundreds of entries through the agent by pasting SQL or media into the dialogue.
- Do not use Cloudflare Browser Rendering (or Puppeteer/Playwright on Workers) for public `t.me` profile pages. Plain HTTP fetch with a browser UA is enough; Browser Rendering spends Cloudflare browser-hours and does not reduce Cursor quota.
- Do not sit in one Cloud Agent for hours watching an import finish.
